    "value": "-17"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(g(x)=ax^7+bx^3+cx,\\) which is odd. Since \\(f(-7)=g(-7)-5=7,\\) \\(g(-7)=12.\\) Therefore \\(g(7)=-12,\\) and \\(f(7)=-12-5=-17.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Separate the constant term from the odd-powered terms",
        "If \\(g(x)=f(x)+5,\\) compare \\(g(7)\\) and \\(g(-7)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
